{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #1110: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $p>q\\geq 2$ be two coprime integers. We call $n$ representable if it is the sum of integers of the form $p^kq^l$, none of which divide each other.\n\nIf $\\{p,q\\}\\neq \\{2,3\\}$ then what can be said about the density of non-representable numbers? Are there infinitely many coprime non-representable numbers? Current best: Yu and Chen \\cite{YuCh22} proved\\[\\frac{n}{(\\log n)^{\\log_23}}\\ll f(n) \\ll \\frac{n}{\\log n}.\\]Yang and Zhao \\cite{YaZh25} improved the lower bound to $f(n)\\gg n/\\log n$. Prize: no. Tags: number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_920562a8dab595e586a09b6e59da77beeaa6163383f1a659c0c16a41832bd410","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:1110","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_9bc4fb732e14ff23","object_root":"sha256:227e60b581f74ee1b41138ff84d43d943f3bacddaab9764f1909baaa52c99a35","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"